# FIRE Agent

FIRE Agent is an independent, benchmark-aligned financial reasoning and
evidence agent. It keeps one unified single-agent runtime and adapts each
benchmark through thin runners, output profiles, scoring projections, and
benchmark-specific evaluators.

All commands below use relative paths and are intended to be run from the
repository root unless the command first enters `fire_agent/`.

## Project Model

FIRE Agent does not import the outer repository runtime and does not read the
outer repository `.env`. It only uses `FIRE_AGENT_*` configuration from
`fire_agent/.env`.

The core flow is:

```text
official benchmark data
  -> FIRE input JSONL
  -> BenchmarkRunner
  -> BenchTaskContext
  -> FIREAgent unified runtime
  -> AgentOutput
  -> benchmark scoring projection
  -> local evaluator or official scorer
```

Current benchmark boundary:

| Bench | Formal FIRE input | Debug-only input | Scoring path |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| FinGAIA | `benchmarks/fingaia.jsonl` | none | official-style LLM judge, `1/0/-1` |
| FinSearchComp | `benchmarks/finsearchcomp.jsonl` | `finsearchcomp_text_20.jsonl`, `finsearchcomp_text_remaining_7.jsonl` | bundled standalone LLM judge |
| FinanceAgentBench | `benchmarks/financeagent_public_full.jsonl`; v2: `benchmarks/financeagent_v2_public_full.jsonl` | `financeagent_public_text_20.jsonl` | local public-rubric evaluator |
| FinRpt | `benchmarks/finrpt.jsonl` | optional sampled FinRpt split | bundled FinRpt `exec_eval.py` |
| FinDocResearch | `benchmarks/findocresearch.jsonl` from official `dataset.csv` | no metadata-QA substitute | local readiness plus OpenFinArena scorer when gold is present |

Do not use `findocresearch_text_20.jsonl`; FinDocResearch is a report-generation
task built from annual-report inputs in the official `dataset.csv`.

## Layout

```text
fire_agent/
  README.md
  pyproject.toml
  requirements.txt
  environment.yml
  .env.example
  docs/
    framework_zh.md
  official_benchmarks/
    fingaia/
