    finrpt/
    findocresearch/
  src/
    fire_agent/
      benchmarks/
        base.py
        common.py
        fingaia.py
        finsearchcomp.py
        financeagentbench.py
        finrpt.py
        findocresearch.py
        registry.py
      evaluators/
        core.py
        common.py
        qa.py
        reports.py
        document_parse.py
        base.py
      aggregation.py
      cli.py
      config.py
      constants.py
      llm.py
      prepare_findocresearch.py
      prepare_finrpt.py
      profiles.py
      renderers.py
      run_benchmarks.py
      runners.py
      runtime.py
      schemas.py
      tool_families.py
```

`runners.py` and `evaluators/base.py` are compatibility facades. New code should
import from `fire_agent.benchmarks` and the split evaluator modules.

## Environment Setup

From the repository root:

```bash
cd fire_agent
conda env create -f environment.yml
conda activate fire-agent
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
python -m pip install -e .
cp .env.example .env
```

If the conda environment already exists:

```bash
cd fire_agent
conda activate fire-agent
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
python -m pip install -e .
```

Pip-only alternative:

```bash
cd fire_agent
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
python -m pip install -e .
cp .env.example .env
```

Fill `fire_agent/.env`:

```text
FIRE_AGENT_MODEL=deepseek-v4-flash
FIRE_AGENT_API_KEY=
FIRE_AGENT_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com

FIRE_AGENT_SERPER_API_KEY=
FIRE_AGENT_JINA_API_KEY=
FIRE_AGENT_ALPHA_VANTAGE_API_KEY=
FIRE_AGENT_SEC_USER_AGENT=fire-agent contact@example.com

FIRE_AGENT_VISION_MODEL=qwen/qwen3.6-plus
FIRE_AGENT_VISION_API_KEY=
FIRE_AGENT_VISION_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
```

For direct module execution without reinstalling after code edits:

```bash
export PYTHONPATH=src
```

## Startup Test

Run these from `fire_agent/`:

```bash
export PYTHONPATH=src
python -m compileall src/fire_agent
python -m fire_agent.cli --help
python -m fire_agent.run_benchmarks --help
python -m fire_agent.prepare_finrpt --help
python -m fire_agent.prepare_findocresearch --help
```

Import smoke test:

```bash
python - <<'PY'
from fire_agent.benchmarks import RUNNER_REGISTRY
from fire_agent.evaluators import get_evaluator

print("benches:", sorted({cls.bench_name for cls in RUNNER_REGISTRY.values()}))
print("finrpt evaluator:", get_evaluator("finrpt").name)
PY
```

One-row runtime smoke test, disabling FIRE agent role model calls. Benchmark
evaluators may still call their own judge models:

```bash
mkdir -p ../output/fire_agent_eval
python -m fire_agent.cli \
  --bench fingaia \
  --infile official_benchmarks/fingaia/data/fingaia.jsonl \
  --outfile ../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_fingaia_heuristic_smoke.jsonl \
  --sample_num 1 \
  --heuristic_only \
  --max_steps 1
```

One-row model smoke test:

```bash
python -m fire_agent.cli \
  --bench fingaia \
  --infile official_benchmarks/fingaia/data/fingaia.jsonl \
  --outfile ../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_fingaia_model_smoke.jsonl \
  --sample_num 1 \
  --max_steps 2
```

## QA Tool YAML Configs

The three QA benchmarks can choose their tool set from YAML files under
`configs/qa/`:

```text
configs/qa/fingaia.yaml
configs/qa/finsearchcomp.yaml
configs/qa/financeagentbench.yaml
```

`fire_agent.cli` auto-loads `configs/qa/<bench>.yaml` when present. Use
`--bench_config path/to/config.yaml` for a single explicit config, or `--tools`
to override the YAML tools from the command line. Batch runs pass the same
directory with `--bench_configs_dir`.

YAML files now use the canonical FIRE Agent tool layer:

```text
web_search        # Serper source discovery; snippets and URLs only
web_reader        # Jina/local non-SEC URL and local file reading
sec_search        # SEC company/filing metadata discovery
sec_reader        # Direct SEC filing text, tables, exhibits, and XBRL reading
market_data       # AkShare structured market data
multimodal_reader # image/video/audio attachment inspection
calculator        # local deterministic arithmetic
```

Benchmark-specific date ceilings, default actions, provider notes, and tool-use
constraints belong in YAML `tool_settings` and `prompt.tool_constraints`. The
old compatibility tool names are no longer registered as Agent-visible tools in
the FIRE runtime.

## Formal Data Import

Run from `fire_agent/`:

```bash
export PYTHONPATH=src
mkdir -p ../benchmarks ../output/fire_agent_eval
```

FinGAIA:

```bash
cp official_benchmarks/fingaia/data/fingaia.jsonl ../benchmarks/fingaia.jsonl
cp official_benchmarks/fingaia/data/standard.jsonl ../benchmarks/fingaia_standard.jsonl
```

FinSearchComp full benchmark:

```bash
cp official_benchmarks/finsearchcomp/data/finsearchcomp.jsonl ../benchmarks/finsearchcomp.jsonl
```

FinanceAgentBench full public benchmark:

```bash
cp official_benchmarks/financeagentbench/data/financeagent_public_full.jsonl ../benchmarks/financeagent_public_full.jsonl
```

FinanceAgent v2 public benchmark:

```bash
python official_benchmarks/financeagentbench/official_eval/prepare_financeagent_benchmark.py \
  --input_csv official_benchmarks/financeagentbench/data/public_v2.csv \
  --output_file official_benchmarks/financeagentbench/data/financeagent_v2_public_full.jsonl \
  --source_dataset finance-agent-v2/data/public.csv \
  --sample_id_prefix financeagent-v2 \
  --missing_answer '' \
  --map_rubric_operator finance_agent_v2_operator=correctness
cp official_benchmarks/financeagentbench/data/financeagent_v2_public_full.jsonl ../benchmarks/financeagent_v2_public_full.jsonl
```

FinRpt, using the bundled prepared split:

```bash
cp official_benchmarks/finrpt/data/finrpt.jsonl ../benchmarks/finrpt.jsonl
```

FinRpt, regenerating from HuggingFace:

```bash
python -m fire_agent.prepare_finrpt \
  --benchmarks_dir ../benchmarks \
  --cache_raw
```

FinDocResearch, using the official `dataset.csv`:

```bash
python -m fire_agent.prepare_findocresearch \
  --dataset_csv official_benchmarks/findocresearch/data/dataset.csv \
  --benchmarks_dir ../benchmarks
```

FinDocResearch with local annual-report PDFs:

```bash
python -m fire_agent.prepare_findocresearch \
  --dataset_csv official_benchmarks/findocresearch/data/dataset.csv \
  --reports_dir official_benchmarks/findocresearch/reports \
  --benchmarks_dir ../benchmarks
```

Verify imported formal inputs:

```bash
wc -l \
  ../benchmarks/fingaia.jsonl \
  ../benchmarks/finsearchcomp.jsonl \
  ../benchmarks/financeagent_public_full.jsonl \
  ../benchmarks/financeagent_v2_public_full.jsonl \
  ../benchmarks/finrpt.jsonl \
  ../benchmarks/findocresearch.jsonl
```

Expected current bundled counts are:

```text
150  fingaia.jsonl
635  finsearchcomp.jsonl
50   financeagent_public_full.jsonl
27   financeagent_v2_public_full.jsonl
20   finrpt.jsonl, unless regenerated full
80   findocresearch.jsonl
```

## Per-Bench Input Smoke Tests

Run from `fire_agent/`:

```bash
python -m fire_agent.cli \
  --bench fingaia \
  --infile ../benchmarks/fingaia.jsonl \
  --outfile ../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_fingaia_smoke.jsonl \
  --sample_num 1

python -m fire_agent.cli \
  --bench finsearchcomp \
  --infile ../benchmarks/finsearchcomp.jsonl \
  --outfile ../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_finsearchcomp_smoke.jsonl \
  --sample_num 1

python -m fire_agent.cli \
  --bench financeagentbench \
  --infile ../benchmarks/financeagent_public_full.jsonl \
  --outfile ../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_financeagentbench_smoke.jsonl \
  --sample_num 1

python -m fire_agent.cli \
  --bench financeagent_v2 \
  --infile ../benchmarks/financeagent_v2_public_full.jsonl \
  --outfile ../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_financeagent_v2_smoke.jsonl \
  --sample_num 1

python -m fire_agent.cli \
  --bench finrpt \
  --infile ../benchmarks/finrpt.jsonl \
  --outfile ../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_finrpt_smoke.jsonl \
  --sample_num 1

python -m fire_agent.cli \
  --bench findocresearch \
  --infile ../benchmarks/findocresearch.jsonl \
  --outfile ../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_findocresearch_smoke.jsonl \
  --sample_num 1
```

## Formal Generation

Run all core benches plus Finance Agent v2:

```bash
python -m fire_agent.run_benchmarks \
  --benchmarks_dir ../benchmarks \
  --output_dir ../output/fire_agent_eval \
  --only fingaia finsearchcomp financeagentbench financeagent_v2 finrpt findocresearch \
  --max_steps 8 \
  --max_tool_calls_per_round 3
```

Resume after interruption:

```bash
python -m fire_agent.run_benchmarks \
  --benchmarks_dir ../benchmarks \
  --output_dir ../output/fire_agent_eval \
  --only fingaia finsearchcomp financeagentbench financeagent_v2 finrpt findocresearch \
  --max_steps 8 \
  --max_tool_calls_per_round 3 \
  --resume
```

Run one bench:

```bash
python -m fire_agent.run_benchmarks \
  --benchmarks_dir ../benchmarks \
  --output_dir ../output/fire_agent_eval \
  --only finsearchcomp \
  --max_steps 8 \
  --max_tool_calls_per_round 3
```

Output files:

```text
../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_fingaia_results.jsonl
../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_finsearchcomp_results.jsonl
../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_financeagent_public_full_results.jsonl
../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_finrpt_results.jsonl
../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_findocresearch_results.jsonl
../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_findocresearch_results/markdown/*.md
```

## Local Summaries

These summaries read the local evaluator metrics embedded in each result JSONL.

```bash
python ../scripts/summarize_fire_results.py \
  --bench fingaia \
  --input ../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_fingaia_results.jsonl \
  --output ../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_fingaia_summary.json

python ../scripts/summarize_fire_results.py \
  --bench finsearchcomp \
  --input ../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_finsearchcomp_results.jsonl \
  --output ../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_finsearchcomp_summary.json

python ../scripts/summarize_fire_results.py \
  --bench financeagentbench \
  --input ../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_financeagent_public_full_results.jsonl \
  --output ../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_financeagentbench_summary.json

python ../scripts/summarize_fire_results.py \
  --bench finrpt \
  --input ../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_finrpt_results.jsonl \
  --output ../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_finrpt_summary.json

python ../scripts/summarize_fire_results.py \
  --bench findocresearch \
  --input ../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_findocresearch_results.jsonl \
  --output ../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_findocresearch_summary.json
```

FinanceAgentBench has no bundled standalone official scorer. Its local score is
the public-rubric LLM-as-judge projection computed by
`FinanceAgentBenchEvaluator`, then summarized by the command above. If no judge
model is configured, FinanceAgentBench rows are marked `judge_unavailable`
without a fallback score.

## Official Or Official-Style Scoring

Load the FIRE Agent environment for judge scripts:

```bash
set -a
source .env
set +a
```

FinGAIA official-style LLM-as-Judge:

```bash
python official_benchmarks/fingaia/official_eval/evaluate_fingaia_llm_judge.py \
  --input_file ../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_fingaia_results.jsonl \
  --output_file ../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_fingaia_judged.jsonl \
  --judge_policy all \
  --max_workers 4

python ../scripts/summarize_fire_results.py \
  --bench fingaia \
  --input ../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_fingaia_judged.jsonl \
  --output ../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_fingaia_judged_summary.json
```

FinSearchComp standalone LLM judge:

```bash
python official_benchmarks/finsearchcomp/official_eval/evaluate_finsearchcomp.py \
  --predictions ../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_finsearchcomp_results.jsonl \
  --reference-data official_benchmarks/finsearchcomp/data/raw/finsearchcomp_data.json \
  --mode llm \
  --judge-model "$FIRE_AGENT_MODEL" \
  --openai-base-url "$FIRE_AGENT_BASE_URL" \
  --openai-api-key "$FIRE_AGENT_API_KEY" \
  --output ../output/fire_agent_eval/fire_finsearchcomp_llm_eval.json
```

FinRpt official scoring runs automatically after FinRpt generation; no batch
official-eval flag is needed:

```bash
python -m fire_agent.run_benchmarks \
  --benchmarks_dir ../benchmarks \
  --output_dir ../output/fire_agent_eval \
  --only finrpt \
  --resume
```

FinDocResearch OpenFinArena scoring uses the external official evaluator and
requires official ground truth under:

```text
official_benchmarks/findocresearch/openfinarena/data/ground_truth/findocresearch_track/markdown/
official_benchmarks/findocresearch/openfinarena/data/ground_truth/findocresearch_track/converted/
```

Then run:

```bash
export OPENAI_API_KEY="$FIRE_AGENT_API_KEY"
export OPENAI_BASE_URL="$FIRE_AGENT_BASE_URL"

python -m fire_agent.run_benchmarks \
  --benchmarks_dir ../benchmarks \
  --output_dir ../output/fire_agent_eval \
  --only findocresearch \
  --resume \
  --run_official_report_eval \
  --openfinarena_competitions_dir official_benchmarks/findocresearch/openfinarena \
  --openfinarena_eval_model "$FIRE_AGENT_MODEL"
```

## Debug Subsets

The following files are retained only for smoke/debug work:

```text
benchmarks/finsearchcomp_text_20.jsonl
benchmarks/finsearchcomp_text_remaining_7.jsonl
benchmarks/financeagent_public_text_20.jsonl
```

They should not be used for benchmark reporting.

## Development Notes

- `benchmarks/` owns benchmark-specific data loading, prompt materialization,
  output projection, and result artifact writing.
- `runtime.py` owns the unified four-role agent flow and does not branch into
  benchmark-specific agents.
- `evaluators/` owns local evaluators and artifact readiness checks.
- `constants.py` keeps shared benchmark constants such as FinRpt official fields
  and FinDocResearch report structure.
- `prepare_finrpt.py` and `prepare_findocresearch.py` prepare official report
  benchmark inputs.
- `run_benchmarks.py` is the preferred batch entrypoint for the five supported
  financial benchmarks.
